From f433d67b6ffbbc474d31c201fa9d8e41df5a1a22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:02:06 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Menu: a pause screen, a settings screen with previews, and a
 game's own look

The menu sized everything from its text, 3.4 % of the window's height, so a
large display showed the same eight rows larger (37 px text at 1080 lines).
Its text is now about 21 px from 800 to 1080 lines and about 2 % of the
height above (Layer::menu_font_size(), Layer::MenuScale); a phone keeps the
old size. The other screens keep theirs.

- A pause screen first: Resume, Settings, Controls, Cheats, Resolution and
  Frame rate in place, Quit game; the game stays in view on the right.
- The settings screen: the six pages behind a tab strip, the rows on the
  left, and a side panel with the focused row's name, description and, for
  some settings, a preview of what it does (ui/menu_look.cpp): the stick's
  dead zone and the value the game reads, full diagonals, trigger point,
  right stick, mouse sensitivity, scaling filter and aspect ratio from the
  paused frame (VulkanRenderer::read_frame, split out of capture_frame),
  font, button prompts and confirm button. The Network page's Status and
  the System page's About move to the panel as cards. RowOptions::key names
  the setting a row changes.
- On the stick's own rows the left stick moves the preview, not the focus
  (Layer::set_left_stick_ignored); the D-pad leaves them.
- GameProfile::theme (InterfaceTheme): the interface's colours, faces and
  title, for every screen of the port's own; PortableKit's brown and gold
  without one. The rows, sections, buttons and hints are drawn in it.
- What the menu says a game does comes from the profile
  (right_stick_camera, mouse_camera, extra_triggers, font_preview_text,
  font_note); the rest names no game: no quests, bows or HD release.
- <prefix>_CLASSIC_MENU=1 draws the panel of before; <prefix>_MENU_TEXT_SIZE
  sets the menu's text size.

Built and run with Dissidia 012 (Windows, clang): every page and preview,
at 1920x1088 and 1440x816, with the input script's virtual gamepad. Not run:
a real pad, Linux, Android, the framework's own build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
